 "/updates/devprayag-railway-station/": {
  "kicker": "Site update · 29 July 2026",
  "h1": "Where the Devprayag railway station has got to",
  "lead": "We went to the station site and filmed what is actually there. Here is the position as it stands, and what it does and does not mean for land prices nearby.",
  "blocks": [
   {
    "t": "video",
    "src": "l117.mp4",
    "poster": "l117.jpg"
   },
   {
    "t": "h",
    "l": 2,
    "x": "What is being built"
   },
   {
    "t": "p",
    "x": "The Rishikesh–Karnaprayag line is a broad-gauge railway being cut through the Garhwal hills, most of it in tunnel. Devprayag is one of the stations on it. The video above was taken at the site, that is the ground as it is now, not a rendering."
   },
   {
    "t": "p",
    "x": "For this belt the significance is simple. Devprayag sits at the bottom of our road, at the confluence, at 475 m. Everything we deal in runs uphill from there to Pauri at 2,000 m. A station at the bottom of that road changes how long it takes someone from Delhi to stand on a plot near the top of it."
   },
   {
    "t": "h",
    "l": 2,
    "x": "What it means for land nearby"
   },
   {
    "t": "p",
    "x": "Land within reach of a station under construction moves before the station opens, and it moves on expectation rather than on use. That is worth saying plainly, because expectation is a thing that can be wrong. Rail projects in this terrain have slipped before, and a plot bought for a station that arrives four years late is money parked, not money working."
   },
   {
    "t": "p",
    "x": "What we would say to anyone considering it: buy the land on what it is worth today with the access it has today. If the station lands on time and the approach roads follow, that is upside you did not pay for. If it slips, you still own a piece of ground that stands on its own merits. Buying purely on the station is a bet, and it should be sized like one."
   },
   {
    "t": "h",
    "l": 2,
    "x": "What we can show you"
   },
   {
    "t": "p",
    "x": "We are on this road. We can tell you where the alignment runs relative to a particular parcel, which approaches are already being cut, and what has actually changed in the last twelve months rather than what was announced."
   },
   {
    "t": "p",
    "x": "We also hold land near the site. Price, size and the document position on those parcels are shared on enquiry rather than published, this pocket is moving, and a figure printed today misleads someone reading it next month."
   }
  ]
 },
